---
number: 508
title: There’s a Garden Where Jesus Is Waiting
common_title: The Beautiful Garden of Prayer
author: Eleanor Allen Schroll
composer: James H. Fillmore
sp_category: "30"
topic: Meditation and Prayer
notes: "AUTO: chorus detected heuristically — verify"
---

[verse 1]
There’s a garden where Jesus is waiting,
There’s a place that is wondrously fair;
For it glows with the light of His presence,
’Tis the beautiful garden of prayer.

[chorus]
O the beautiful garden, the garden of prayer!
O the beautiful garden of prayer!
There my Saviour awaits, and He opens the gates
To the beautiful garden of prayer.

[verse 2]
There’s a garden where Jesus is waiting,
And I go with my burden and care
Just to learn from His lips words of comfort,
In the beautiful garden of prayer.

[chorus]
O the beautiful garden, the garden of prayer!
O the beautiful garden of prayer!
There my Saviour awaits, and He opens the gates
To the beautiful garden of prayer.

[verse 3]
There’s a garden where Jesus is waiting,
And He bids you to come meet Him there;
Just to bow, and receive a new blessing,
In the beautiful garden of prayer.

[chorus]
O the beautiful garden, the garden of prayer!
O the beautiful garden of prayer!
There my Saviour awaits, and He opens the gates
To the beautiful garden of prayer.
